# Storage and AI attachments

## Storage abstraction

- Use **`storageService`** for uploads, deletes, URLs, buffers — not ad hoc `fs` in controllers/services that must run in Cloud Run.
- **Production:** `STORAGE_PROVIDER=gcs` with project/bucket env vars; ADC on Cloud Run (no key file required in the standard setup).
- **Local:** `STORAGE_PROVIDER=local` and `LOCAL_UPLOAD_DIR` as configured.

## AI vision and attachments

- When attachments exist, ensure the vision pipeline (e.g. `getVisionImageParts` / **visionImageParts**) reaches the provider — text-only requests never “see” images.
- **Do not assume** a persistent **`/uploads`** tree on Cloud Run. Resolve paths/URLs and read via **GCS + `storageService`** (`resolveStoragePath`, `getFileBuffer`, etc.).
- Prefer **GCS fetch + `/tmp` or in-memory** steps for transforms (e.g. PDF→image); clean up temp files.
- New providers: declare capabilities in `server/src/ai/providers/capabilities.ts`; use a **vision-capable** model when images are present.
- Log with **`[VISION_PIPELINE]`**: file counts, vision part counts, model id, multimodal vs text-only. See `docs/ai/RUNBOOK.md` and `docs/ai/GOLDEN_RULES.md`.

